{"tool_name":"bioconductor-genomautomorphism","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"bioconductor-genomautomorphism","home":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/GenomAutomorphism","license":"Artistic-2.0","summary":"This is a R package to compute the automorphisms between pairwise aligned DNA sequences represented as elements from a Genomic Abelian group. In a general scenario, from genomic regions till the whole genomes from a given population (from any species or close related species) can be algebraically represented as a direct sum of cyclic groups or more specifically Abelian p-groups. Basically, we propose the representation of multiple sequence alignments of length N bp as element of a finite Abelian group created by the direct sum of homocyclic Abelian group of prime-power order.","addition_date":"2026-08-30T02:42:36.700019Z","last_update_date":"2026-08-30T02:42:36.703331Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Library"],"version":["1.14.1"],"collections":["BioConductor"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:bioconductor-genomautomorphism","credit":[{"name":"Robersy Sanchez","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer","Maintainer"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["User manual"],"url":"https://bioconductor.org/packages/GenomAutomorphism"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"name":"GenomAutomorphism","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"gh2biotools","publication":[{"doi":"10.18129/B9.bioc.GenomAutomorphism"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"GenomAutomorphism","home":"https://bio.tools/bioconductor-genomautomorphism","license":"Artistic-2.0","version":"1.14.1","summary":"This is a R package to compute the automorphisms between pairwise aligned DNA sequences represented as elements from a Genomic Abelian group. In a general scenario, from genomic regions till the whole genomes from a given population (from any species or close related species) can be algebraically represented as a direct sum of cyclic groups or more specificall